---
// /stamps/ — THE FORWARDER.
//
// The founder, 2026-08-30: the Town page absorbs Stamps entirely. So the portal
// MOVED to /town/ — every block of it, byte for byte — and this route stays
// alive because a path is an API for consumers the repo cannot reach. Letters
// in the town's own record link /stamps/#board. The connector's answers link it.
// Whatever anyone bookmarked links it. NOTHING MAY 404, and nothing may land on
// a page that no longer has the thing they asked for.
//
// ── WHY A PAGE AND NOT A CONFIG REDIRECT ─────────────────────────────────────
// astro.config.town.mjs's `redirects` map matches PATHS, and a fragment never
// reaches the server — so a config redirect can send /stamps/ to /town/ and
// will silently drop the #board a reader actually asked for. The whole value of
// this route is the fragment, so the forwarding has to happen where the
// fragment exists, which is the browser.
//
// ── THE ANCHOR MAP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Nearly an identity, and deliberately so. When the portal's blocks moved they
// KEPT THEIR IDS — #board, #pots, #numbers, #rules and all nine teaching ids
// are the same words on the hub as they were here — because a rename would have
// stranded every deep link ever written to save a hyphen. Exactly one fragment
// needed mapping: #market, the old Market tab, whose two blocks are now the
// Bounty Board lane and the pots block inside the rules; it lands on the board.
//
// ── AND IT WORKS WITH NO JAVASCRIPT ──────────────────────────────────────────
// Two mechanisms, in this order. The inline script runs first and carries the
// fragment; if scripting is off, the <meta refresh> below still lands the
// reader on the hub — at its top rather than at their block, which is a
// degraded arrival rather than a dead one. The visible body is the third
// fallback: an ordinary link, for anything that honours neither.
const HUB = "/town/";
// the one fragment whose name changed; everything else forwards as-is
const REMAP = { market: "board" };
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Stamps has moved to The Town — Postmark</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href={HUB} />
    {/* a forwarder is not a page anyone should land on from a search result */}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />

    {/* FIRST, because it is the one that keeps the fragment. `replace` rather
        than `assign` so the Back button returns to wherever the reader came
        from instead of bouncing them through the forwarder again. */}
    <script is:inline define:vars={{ HUB, REMAP }}>
      (function () {
        var id = decodeURIComponent((location.hash || "").slice(1));
        var to = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(REMAP, id) ? REMAP[id] : id;
        location.replace(HUB + (to ? "#" + encodeURIComponent(to) : ""));
      })();
    </script>

    {/* SECOND, for a reader with no scripting. It cannot carry the fragment —
        that is not a bug here, it is the reason the script is above it. */}
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content={`0; url=${HUB}`} />

    <style>
      body {
        background: #070b15; color: #cdc2ab;
        font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Consolas, monospace;
        display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
        min-height: 100vh; margin: 0; padding: 2rem; text-align: center;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }
      a { color: #e8c48b; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>
      Stamps is now part of <a href={HUB}>The Town</a> — the town's civic quarter,
      with the market, the dials and the whole teaching in it.
      <br />
      <a href={HUB}>Continue to The Town →</a>
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
